//@version=6
strategy("W5 M2 POOC short opening call (comm 0.05 slip 1)", overlay=true, process_orders_on_close=true, commission_type=strategy.commission.percent, commission_value=0.05, slippage=1)

// Lane W5-ENG-MARGIN-V6, mechanism M2 (the opening call). A 100%-of-equity
// SHORT process_orders_on_close fills one tick under a signal close, and the
// entry's commission leaves it short of margin. The next bar opens one tick
// above that close, at it, or one tick below. At which price does TradingView
// size its call there -- the signal close or the open -- and does it call
// again at its own slipped fill?
if time == timestamp("UTC", 2025, 4, 2, 0, 0)
    strategy.entry("S", strategy.short, comment="short")
if time == timestamp("UTC", 2025, 4, 2, 0, 0) + 30 * 60000
    strategy.close_all(comment="cleanup")
if time == timestamp("UTC", 2025, 4, 2, 3, 0)
    strategy.entry("S", strategy.short, comment="short")
if time == timestamp("UTC", 2025, 4, 2, 3, 0) + 30 * 60000
